{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the second documentation follow-up at head b02fe46b, tree 27038184, for review request a1e86582. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nI read section 7 of the review record, the three repairs from c271830a at this head, and how the merge carried main's additions. Only documents differ from main ada88648, and `git merge-tree --write-tree` of the two gives this head's tree.\n\n## The three repairs\n\n1. `docs/security/settings.md:98` now names the three default cohorts: `archive-device-publication`, `unpublished` and `commons`.\n2. A search of `write-an-application.md`, `self-host.md` and `trust-boundaries.md` finds no \"family\" left, and `settings.md` uses \"cohort\". `ten-terms.md` says \"created\".\n3. `what-is-dap.md:150` names the invitation link and the configuration file and key.\n\n## How the merge carried main's additions\n\nMy own count differs from yours, and the difference is harmless. Taking the merge base with dfe69293, c8c7b631, I find 273 added lines and 52 not verbatim, where you report 27. The extra lines are the rewrapped ones in `kernel.md`, `mcp.md` and `scopes.md`, which my line match can't follow. So I checked meaning and not lines, on the facts that matter most:\n\n- Kernel section 7.4 holds every rule from main that I compared: the five reads, the contract additions, the wire exports, the wait staying in Scope, no journal entry or alarm, the retained hash at or above the floor, `unavailable` on a missing or different hash, no hash check below the floor, and `behind` only after authority checks.\n- `docs/mcp.md` holds the seven omissions, twenty names, the Membership pin split, the clock statement, the walk's null `next`, `omittedScopes`, the first-window rule for `work`, the room text sentence and the finding reads.\n- `docs/security/settings.md` names the seven omissions and \"no more than 20 items\". `entry-points.md` carries the list too.\n- The views section now says five reads, which matches its table and corrects main's \"four\". The index has a row for that page.\n- The inconclusive-result text is in `testing.md`.\n\nI sampled these facts and did not compare all 52 lines one by one.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- `security-settings.test.mjs` and `security-entry-points.test.mjs` pass 13 of 13. `check-doc-links` finds 976 links with 0 broken, `check-commit-messages` checks 7 with 0 flagged, and the worktree stayed clean.\n- The evidence verifies: 16 files with none writable, and `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 669b9346.\n- `check-notes` gives one warning: `2026-10-30-docs-relocated-text.md` is 125,378 bytes, over the 40,960 limit. That note keeps moved text as landed, and I accept it as a record. Say so if anyone asks why the warning stays.\n\nThe gate did not run, and I accept that under the documents-only rule. I ran no independent second read, and I didn't re-review the rewrite's earlier items, which my 4f2e8b24 and c271830a cover.\n\n## For the planner\n\nLand this soon. Main's next heads change these same pages: the earlier-version answer changes `docs/mcp.md`, and J1 will too. Whichever lands second has to carry the other's words by hand, as this merge did.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: no code, no conclusion needed.\n- Security: approved. The security pages state the defaults that the code uses.\n- Simplification: approved.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:944abfe303e6739bd7e30e6d8ab991b3469cb731","binding":"assigned","head":"b02fe46b46c01ed74ec3586e83b0f6c60eee7fa2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:74083ad8aa380061214d29051d5799b595b32206\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:547c0c7f376a47d7ed48158feab9ebc7c6f79fec\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:74083ad8aa380061214d29051d5799b595b32206","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}